.\" sliver-agent(1). Prose: docs/agent.md, docs/api.md.
.TH SLIVER\-AGENT 1 2026-10-12 "sliver 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sliver\-agent \- per\-user Touch Bar session agent
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sliver\-agent
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-socket
.IR path ]
.br
.B sliver\-agent \-\-render
.I prefix
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-size
.IR W x H ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sliver\-agent
decides what the Touch Bar shows for the logged\-in user.
It reads the configuration
.RB ( sliver\-config (5))
and the stylesheet
.RB ( sliver\-stylesheet (5)),
follows the focused app, workspace and session state, runs the modules, renders frames, and hands them to
.BR sliverd (8),
which owns the hardware.
It also serves the public session D\-Bus API
.RI ( io.github.wawow830.Sliver ),
which
.BR sliverctl (1)
and any other app or script can use to publish items and control the bar.
.PP
The agent runs unprivileged as a systemd user service in the graphical session.
If it is not running, crashes or hangs,
.B sliverd
shows its built\-in F\-key layer, so Escape and the F\-keys always keep working.
.PP
Esc, F\-keys and other plain key buttons are sent to
.B sliverd
as key regions.
.B sliverd
presses them directly, so they never wait on the agent.
Everything else (sliders, gestures, widgets) is handled by the agent.
.PP
Nothing is rendered unless something changed.
While the bar is off, the agent doesn't render and the modules' timers stop.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " file"
Use this configuration instead of searching the standard paths.
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " path"
Path of
.BR sliverd 's
socket.
The default is
.I /run/sliver/sliverd.sock
or
.BR $SLIVER_SOCKET .
.TP
.BI \-\-render " prefix"
Headless mode: write
.IB prefix \-base.png
and
.IB prefix \-fn.png
with what the bar would show, print every module cell (rectangle, id, CSS classes, content), and exit.
.B sliverd
is not needed.
.TP
.BI \-\-size " W\fBx\fPH"
Bar size for
.BR \-\-render .
The default is 2008x60.
.TP
.B \-\-replace
Take the public D\-Bus name from an agent that is already running, for example to try a
development build.
The running agent steps back from the bar and takes it again when this one exits.
Without this option, a second agent prints why and exits with status 1, so it never takes the
bar or the name from the installed agent.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.BI SIGRTMIN+ n
Re\-run every module configured with
.BI "signal = " n
(like waybar).
.TP
.B SIGUSR2
Reload the configuration (see BUGS).
.TP
.B SIGUSR1
Toggle the whole bar, like waybar's
.B on\-sigusr1
(see BUGS).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sliver/config.toml
User configuration.
See
.BR sliver\-config (5)
for the full search path.
.TP
.I ~/.config/sliver/style.css
User stylesheet.
.TP
.I /run/sliver/sliverd.sock
.BR sliverd 's
socket.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SLIVER_SOCKET
Default for
.BR \-\-socket .
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Where the user configuration lives (default
.IR ~/.config ).
.PP
Commands run by modules get
.BR SLIVER_MODULE ,
.BR SLIVER_LAYER ,
.B SLIVER_LAYOUT
and
.BR SLIVER_APP_ID .
.SH BUGS
Version 0.1.0 is a development snapshot.
Hot reload of the configuration
.RB ( SIGUSR2 ,
inotify),
.B SIGUSR1
are still being wired up.
Of the
.BR sliverctl (1)
control commands,
.BR layout ,
.BR profile ,
.BR reload ,
.BR show / hide / toggle
of single modules and
.B update
are not supported yet.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sliverctl (1),
.BR sliver\-config (5),
.BR sliver\-stylesheet (5),
.BR sliverd (8)
.PP
.I docs/agent.md
and
.I docs/api.md
in the sliver sources.
